    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d921">

                <pb facs="1003" n="911" xml:id="pg911"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 761.91/55</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Persia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-13T18:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 13, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>75. Your 10 a.m., August 1, and 11 a.m., August 4, and Department’s 6 p.m.,
                    August 7. Ascertain discreetly and report fully and promptly attitude all
                    foreign legations, particularly German, Austrian and Turkish, relative to decree
                    of Persian Cabinet. Department desires to receive all possible facts and
                    suggestions relative to this matter. Instruct Southard also to investigate and report his views.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
